<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεία</span></b>  (B), 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληΐη</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾴα</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>O.</u>
			10(11).44
		</span></i>), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>booty, plunder</i>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
			</span></i> (v. infr.), etc. (<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i> always use <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληΐς</span>); esp. of
			cattle, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωποι</span>, Pi.l.c.,
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.94
			</span></i> (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείας ἀπαρχὴν βοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					761
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				145
			</span></i> (anap.): pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφθαρμένας
				εὑρίσκομεν λείας ἁπάσας</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i>; rarely of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγόμεθα λεία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					614
				</span></i>
			; <i>prey</i> of hunters, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				326
			</span></i>: generally, <i>booty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.2.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1.3.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς λοιποὺς ληΐην
			θέσθαι</span> give them up <i>as plunder</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.202
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείαν ποιεῖσθαι τὴν χώραν,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λεηλατεῖν τὴν χώραν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.41
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λείαν ἄγειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					5.3.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ λείαν ἐκπορεύσονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.1.8
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ ληΐην ἐκπλῶσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.152
				</span></i>
			: pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διεσκεδασμένοι κατὰ τὰς ἰδίας λείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					1.2.5
				</span></i>
			: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μυσῶν λεία</span>, of
			anything that may be plundered with impunity, <i><span class="en">
				Stratt.
				35
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1372b33
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>plunder</i> (as an act), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῶσι ἀπὸ ληΐης καὶ πολέμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.103
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>stolen property</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν λ. ἀποδοῦναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					145.16
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.438.10
			</span></i>-<i><span class="en">
				13
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>flocks and herds, cattle</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπογραφὴ λείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PHib.</u>
					1.33.2
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				3p.279
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1012
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				19.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				97
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέλεια τῆς λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					748.9
				</span></i>
			 (Cyzic., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>). (Lit. <i>the people's
				property</i>, cf. Lat. <i>populari</i> 'plunder'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
